  "deck": "Jorrel Hato's 9 points led a Bin XI that scored 73, more than any side in the league.",
  "body": "Jorrel Hato tops the bin. Chelsea won 2-0 away to Everton and the defender took an assist and a clean sheet from it across 90 minutes, with a tackle won and a clearance beside them.\n\nThe back is clean sheets throughout. Zion Suzuki kept one in goal in Aston Villa's 1-0 win away to Newcastle United, after Hazza Maguazza's Redempshazza dropped him ahead of the gameweek. Fulham's 1-0 over Hull City puts Calvin Bassey, Antonee Robinson and Timothy Castagne in the same line, with Adam Smith beside them from AFC Bournemouth's 2-0 against Sunderland. The middle is two clean sheets and a goal: Boubacar Kamara for the Villans, Tyler Adams for the Cherries, and James Maddison scoring in Tottenham Hotspur's 3-1 win over Coventry City. Up front Omar Marmoush scored in that same match, and Daizen Maeda scored in Ipswich Town's 3-2 defeat away to Manchester City.",
